{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROOT CAUSE (widening was insufficient — reopened). Live run 33042729934: DC lane FAILED again. Both rich-text tests hit 'the index never reflected the pushed body within 240s (120 attempts)' — indexed description stayed None at creation-time. This run the whole DC step ran ~2x normal (~100min), i.e. the ephemeral instance's background reindex thread was starved. Per ADR 0037 §3 the DC index lag is UNBOUNDED, so NO fixed timeout is robust — the Aug-24 green run only got lucky at ~85s. Sibling suites that wait on labels/summary passed, confirming it is the starved background reindex, not a returned-field problem. NEW FIX: force a synchronous per-issue reindex (POST /rest/api/2/reindex/issue?issueId=..., admin, Jira 8.17.1) after each description write so the JQL search reflects deterministically; keep the existing wait as fast confirmation and as a safe fallback if the endpoint 404s (no regression). Cloud mutation lane GREEN this run."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787815974048616001,"uuid":"c19285f7-9d9a-45a9-acc1-65a66be3387c"}